**What changed**
- `src/intervals.ts` — implemented `mergeIntervals`: validates every pair first (throws `RangeError` with the offending pair, e.g. `[5, 3]`), then sorts a shallow copy by start (ties by end), and folds into the result, merging when the next start is ≤ the current merged end, so overlaps and touches (end == start) both merge. New `[start, end]` pairs are pushed, so neither the input array nor its pairs are mutated.
- `src/intervals.test.ts` — 9 tests: overlap, touch, nested, out-of-order input, chains of touches, duplicates/points/empty/negative-fractional, no-mutation of input and its pairs, and the `RangeError` (type + message naming the pair).

